XGBoost in depth: 
Gradient Boosting: 
Starts with the first function. Then takes the residuals (actual value - predicted). splits the dataset and takes the mean of those. 
The end result will be the sum of the results from all the previous decision trees
![alt text](image.png)

To find where to split the leaves: 
similarity score = (sum of residuals)^2 / (# residuals + lambda)
lambda = regularization parameter to prevent overfitting

Sleft, Sright, Gain = Sleft + Sright - Sroot


Mean squared error (MSE) - loss function

is another field of study in which machine learning analysis is used to decrease congestion in urban settings.
